{"Debug log.Error calls left in production cleanup code - six logging calls in CleanAnnotations and CleanOrphanedAnnotationTags use r.log.Error() for routine informational messages like 'Annotations to clean by time' and 'cleaned annotations by time', which will flood error logs and potentially trigger alerting systems": 0.9720368385314941, "Cleanup service ticker interval reduced from 10 minutes to 1 minute, causing all cleanup jobs to run 10x more frequently and significantly increasing database load": 0.9375337958335876, "Log calls dump all annotation IDs into log output (e.g., 'ids', ids), which could produce very large log entries for big batches": 0.95360267162323, "With 1-minute ticker but 9-minute timeout still in place, cleanup jobs taking longer than 1 minute will cause the next tick to buffer and fire immediately, effectively running cleanup back-to-back": 0.7365077137947083}